From eadf46d0ec330b332a413bea78235dea950f02db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:12:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 20/28] feat: implement
 VK_EXT_dynamic_rendering_unused_attachments

Problem: Undefined draws when PSO RTV/DSV formats differ from the bound targets; vkd3d-proton warns the extension "is required for correct operation".

Root cause: D3D12 allows a pipeline to write a slot with nothing bound, or to leave a bound target undeclared. Metal requires pipeline formats to equal the render pass attachments, and vkd3d-proton has no fallback without this extension.

Fix: MVKGraphicsPipeline keeps its final render pipeline descriptor. At draw time (prepareDraw) the bound subpass formats are compared; when only presence differs, a variant is compiled and cached per (pipeline, bound presence): bound-but-undeclared slots get the bound format with writeMask None, declared-but-unbound slots get no format, depth/stencil follow the bound attachments, retrying with the pipeline's own depth/stencil when the shader writes them. Plain pipelines only; tessellation, mesh and multiview keep the old behaviour. Extension and feature advertised.

Verified by: test_unused_attachments_mix_and_match 1978 -> 0 failures; test_null_rtv and test_unbound_rtv_rendering pass; test_renderpass_rendering 0 errors.

Off switch: none
